From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kanaka Raju Nayana <kanaka.raju.nayana@intel.com>
Date: Thu, 2 Jul 2026 17:13:11 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] vfio/type1: handle missing follow_pfnmap_args.addr_mask on
 velinux 5.15

vfio_iommu_type1.c uses follow_pfnmap_args.addr_mask to compute PFNMAP range size.
On velinux 5.15.198, the 6.12 follow_pfnmap API was cherry-picked, but the
later 6.15 struct update adding addr_mask was not, so compilation
fails with missing member errors.

Use PAGE_MASK as fallback in VFIO type1. PAGE_MASK is safe here because it forces
single-page granularity for range calculation, which is conservative and avoids
incorrect contiguous PFN expansion while preserving correctness.

Signed-off-by: Kanaka Raju Nayana <kanaka.raju.nayana@intel.com>
---
 drivers/vfio/vfio_iommu_type1.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/vfio/vfio_iommu_type1.c b/drivers/vfio/vfio_iommu_type1.c
index 4684cdd9f..a6b92ae90 100644
--- a/drivers/vfio/vfio_iommu_type1.c
+++ b/drivers/vfio/vfio_iommu_type1.c
@@ -547,7 +547,11 @@ static int follow_fault_pfn(struct vm_area_struct *vma, struct mm_struct *mm,
 		ret = -EFAULT;
 	} else {
 		*pfn = args.pfn;
+#ifdef BPM_FOLLOW_PFNMAP_ARGS_ADDR_MASK_NOT_PRESENT
+		*addr_mask = PAGE_MASK;
+#else
 		*addr_mask = args.addr_mask;
+#endif
 	}
 
 	follow_pfnmap_end(&args);
-- 
